First of all, if you are blind and in a place where you aren't being 
attacked in a store, you shouldn't try moving around.  Instead, hit the . 
key to rest, or alternatively hit "n" followed by a number then the . key 
to rest N number of times.

Since you were dumb enough to attack the storekeeper your options as I 
see them are as follows:

1) You could kill the storekeeper.  At level 10 this won't be easy.  You 
would need some really good wands, weapons, or spells.  I've done it 
before, but in general at level 10 the shopkeeper will probably kill you 
instead.

2) Pay the storekeeper some money to make him happy.  Think of it like, 
you just made a friend angry.  Imagine how happy he would be if you gave 
him $1000.

3) Avoid the storekeeper entirely.  One thing you could "try" is 
teleporting the storekeeper with a wand of teleport if you have one.  I 
don't recommend doing that though because you don't know where the 
storekeeper is going to end up.  He could end up near the exit to the 
level.

I would say that 2 is your best option.  If you really have some powerful 
stuff, you could do 1.  Sometimes the storekeeper has some good items on 
him.  However, killing the storekeeper will bring you disfavor with the 
gods, which can easily be remedied by sacrificing some corpses on the 
altars.




